PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L02U1.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":2,"cefr":"A1b","unit":1,"theme":"My Daily Routine","essential_question":"How does a good routine help us every day?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1","title":"Yusuf's Busy Day: The Present Simple","objectives":["Students will be able to use the present simple to talk about routines and facts.","Students will be able to add -s or -es to verbs after he, she and it.","I can talk about my daily routine.","I can say \"He gets up at six\" with -s."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام المضارع البسيط للحديث عن العادات والحقائق.","سيتمكن الطلاب من إضافة s أو es للفعل بعد he وshe وit.","أستطيع أن أتحدث عن روتيني اليومي.","أستطيع أن أقول He gets up at six مع إضافة s."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"wake up","pos":"phrasal verb","ipa":"/weɪk ʌp/","definition":"to stop sleeping","arabic":"يستيقظ","example":"I wake up when the sun comes up.","image_id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS1-W01"},{"word":"get dressed","pos":"verb phrase","ipa":"/ɡɛt drɛst/","definition":"to put on your clothes","arabic":"يرتدي ملابسه","example":"Rakan gets dressed in five minutes.","image_id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS1-W02"},{"word":"breakfast","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbrɛkfəst/","definition":"the first meal of the day","arabic":"الفطور","example":"We have eggs and bread for breakfast.","image_id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS1-W03"},{"word":"brush","pos":"verb","ipa":"/brʌʃ/","definition":"to clean something with a brush","arabic":"يُنظّف بالفرشاة","example":"Brush your teeth for two minutes.","image_id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use the present simple for things we do again and again (routines and habits) and for facts: I get up at six. The sun rises in the east.\nWith he, she, it and one person, add -s to the verb: he plays, she reads, it starts. With I, you, we, they, use the base verb: I play, they read.\nSome verbs add -es: go → goes, do → does, watch → watches, brush → brushes. have → has (special!).\nI / you / we / they + base verb: We walk to school.\nhe / she / it + verb + -s/-es: She walks to school.\nhave → has; go → goes; do → does.","examples":["I wake up at half past five.","My dad drives to work.","We pray Fajr with our grandfather.","The bus leaves at a quarter to seven.","Noura reads a story at bedtime.","My brothers watch cartoons on Friday.","The library opens at eight.","Grandma has tea after lunch."],"common_errors":["✗ He play football after school. → ✓ He plays football after school. (he/she/it → add -s.)","✗ She is go to school by bus. → ✓ She goes to school by bus. (Don't add is to the present simple.)","✗ They gets up early. → ✓ They get up early. (they → no -s.)","✗ My father have breakfast at six. → ✓ My father has breakfast at six. (he/she → has.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم المضارع البسيط للعادات اليومية والحقائق: I get up at six.\nمع he وshe وit والمفرد نضيف s أو es للفعل: He plays / She watches.\nلا نضيف is قبل الفعل: She goes (وليس She is go).\nhave مع المفرد الغائب تصبح has، وgo تصبح goes، وdo تصبح does."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Yusuf's Busy Day: The Present Simple”. Let’s learn present simple affirmative (I play / he plays) together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U1-LS1 | Yusuf's Busy Day: The Present Simple","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Yusuf's Busy Day”: Yusuf wakes up at six o'clock every day. He gets dressed and brushes his teeth. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Yusuf wakes up at six o'clock every day. He gets dressed and brushes his teeth.","visual":"Image GV-L02-U1-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use the present simple for things we do again and again (routines and habits) and for facts: I get up at six. The sun rises in the east. With he, she, it and one person, add -s to the verb: he plays, she reads, it starts. With I, you, we, they, use the base verb: I play, they read.","on_screen":"I / you / we / they + base verb: We walk to school. • he / she / it + verb + -s/-es: She walks to school. • have → has; go → goes; do → does.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I wake up at half past five. My dad drives to work. We pray Fajr with our grandfather.","on_screen":"I wake up at half past five. / My dad drives to work. / We pray Fajr with our grandfather.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “He play football after school.” That’s not right. We say: “He plays football after school.” he/she/it → add -s.","on_screen":"✗ He play football after school.   ✓ He plays football after school.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"Yusuf goes to bed at nine.\" Does he do this one time or every day? … Think! … Every day – it's a routine. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about my daily routine.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can talk about my daily routine.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present simple affirmative (I play / he plays).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم المضارع البسيط للعادات اليومية والحقائق: I get up at six.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: He play football after school. — الصحيح: He plays football after school.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتحدث عن روتيني اليومي."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Yusuf's Busy Day","body":"Yusuf wakes up at six o'clock every day. He gets dressed and brushes his teeth.\nThen he has breakfast with his family. His mother makes eggs and bread.\nYusuf goes to school by bus. Lessons start at seven.\nAfter school, he does his homework and plays football with his cousins.\nThe family eats dinner at eight. Yusuf goes to bed at nine.\nHe loves his busy day!","word_count":67,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"My sister ___ to school at seven.","options":["going","is go","goes","go"],"answer":"goes","explanation":"Verbs ending in o, sh, ch, x → add -es (goes, watches).","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المنتهية بـ o وsh وch وx تأخذ es."},{"q":"We ___ lunch at twelve.","options":["having","haves","have","has"],"answer":"have","explanation":"I / you / we / they → base verb (no -s).","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey الفعل بدون s."},{"q":"The lesson ___ at nine o'clock.","options":["starts","starting","is start","start"],"answer":"starts","explanation":"he / she / it → verb + -s.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نضيف s للفعل."},{"q":"Dad ___ the news every evening.","options":["watch","watches","watching","watchs"],"answer":"watches","explanation":"Verbs ending in o, sh, ch, x → add -es (goes, watches).","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المنتهية بـ o وsh وch وx تأخذ es."},{"q":"I ___ my bed every morning.","options":["making","is make","makes","make"],"answer":"make","explanation":"I / you / we / they → base verb (no -s).","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey الفعل بدون s."},{"q":"Omar ___ a big glass of milk for breakfast.","options":["have","having","haves","has"],"answer":"has","explanation":"he / she / it → has (not haves).","explanation_ar":"have تصبح has مع المفرد الغائب."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the correct form of the verb. Word bank: opens, feeds, live","items":[{"q":"Lina ______ (feed) her cat every morning.","options":[],"answer":"feeds","explanation":"he / she / it → verb + -s.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نضيف s للفعل."},{"q":"My cousins ______ (live) in Jeddah.","options":[],"answer":"live","explanation":"I / you / we / they → base verb (no -s).","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey الفعل بدون s."},{"q":"The baker ______ (open) his shop at five.","options":[],"answer":"opens","explanation":"he / she / it → verb + -s.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نضيف s للفعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-B2","type":"order","instructions":"Guided practice: Put the words in order.","items":[{"q":"Fahad / breakfast / his / brushes / after / teeth   ( . )","options":["Fahad","breakfast","his","brushes","after","teeth"],"answer":"Fahad brushes his teeth after breakfast.","explanation":"Word order: Verbs ending in o, sh, ch, x → add -es (goes, watches).","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: الأفعال المنتهية بـ o وsh وch وx تأخذ es."},{"q":"to / the / together / mosque / We / walk   ( . )","options":["to","the","together","mosque","We","walk"],"answer":"We walk to the mosque together.","explanation":"Word order: I / you / we / they → base verb (no -s).","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: مع I وyou وwe وthey الفعل بدون s."},{"q":"The / at / ten / finishes / film   ( . )","options":["The","at","ten","finishes","film"],"answer":"The film finishes at ten.","explanation":"Word order: Verbs ending in o, sh, ch, x → add -es (goes, watches).","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: الأفعال المنتهية بـ o وsh وch وx تأخذ es."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about your routine.","items":[{"q":"I wake up at ___.","options":[],"answer":"I wake up at six o'clock.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple affirmative (I play / he plays) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"For breakfast, I have ___.","options":[],"answer":"For breakfast, I have cheese and bread.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple affirmative (I play / he plays) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My mom/dad ___ every morning.","options":[],"answer":"My dad drives to work every morning.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple affirmative (I play / he plays) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"After school, I ___.","options":[],"answer":"After school, I do my homework.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple affirmative (I play / he plays) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In the evening, my family ___.","options":[],"answer":"In the evening, my family eats dinner together.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple affirmative (I play / he plays) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write about a person's day.","items":[{"q":"Write 4 sentences about your own day from morning to night.","options":[],"answer":"I get up at six. I go to school by car. I play football after school. I go to bed at nine.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple affirmative (I play / he plays) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Interview a partner. Write 3 sentences about his day with he.","options":[],"answer":"Saad gets up at five thirty. He has breakfast at six. He walks to school.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple affirmative (I play / he plays) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 facts about animals with the present simple.","options":[],"answer":"Owls sleep in the day. A cow gives milk.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple affirmative (I play / he plays) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Four Corners Grammar","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a sentence frame with a cue word and four possible answers (A–D).","Students walk to the corner with the correct answer.","One student in each corner explains the choice in one sentence.","Correct corner scores a point; continue with the next cue."],"data":[{"label":"I"},{"label":"my mom"},{"label":"Omar"},{"label":"we"},{"label":"my cousins"},{"label":"the bus"},{"label":"you"},{"label":"my grandpa"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"My brother ___ his homework after lunch.","options":["do","does","doing","dos"],"answer":"does","explanation":"Verbs ending in o, sh, ch, x → add -es (goes, watches).","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المنتهية بـ o وsh وch وx تأخذ es."},{"q":"They ___ in a big house.","options":["living","is live","lives","live"],"answer":"live","explanation":"I / you / we / they → base verb (no -s).","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey الفعل بدون s."},{"q":"The sun ___ in the east.","options":["is rise","rises","rising","rise"],"answer":"rises","explanation":"he / she / it → verb + -s.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نضيف s للفعل."},{"q":"My aunt ___ two cats.","options":["is have","have","has","haves"],"answer":"has","explanation":"he / she / it → has (not haves).","explanation_ar":"have تصبح has مع المفرد الغائب."},{"q":"","options":["He play chess on Friday.","He is play chess on Friday.","He plays chess on Friday.","He playing chess on Friday."],"answer":"He plays chess on Friday.","explanation":"Don't use am/is/are before a present simple verb.","explanation_ar":"لا نضع is قبل فعل المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"You ___ very good tea, Grandma!","options":["make","makes","is make","making"],"answer":"make","explanation":"I / you / we / they → base verb (no -s).","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey الفعل بدون s."},{"q":"The baby ___ a lot.","options":["cries","crys","cry","crying"],"answer":"cries","explanation":"Verbs ending in o, sh, ch, x → add -es (goes, watches).","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المنتهية بـ o وsh وch وx تأخذ es."},{"q":"","options":["My parents is wake up early.","My parents wakes up early.","My parents waking up early.","My parents wake up early."],"answer":"My parents wake up early.","explanation":"I / you / we / they → base verb (no -s).","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey الفعل بدون s."},{"q":"Our teacher ___ English very well.","options":["speaking","speaks","speakes","speak"],"answer":"speaks","explanation":"he / she / it → verb + -s.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نضيف s للفعل."},{"q":"","options":["The shop closes at ten.","The shop is close at ten.","The shop close at ten.","The shop closing at ten."],"answer":"The shop closes at ten.","explanation":"he / she / it → verb + -s.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نضيف s للفعل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"A comic strip of Yusuf's morning: waking up at 6:00, brushing his teeth, eating breakfast with his family and getting on the yellow school bus. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A comic strip of Yusuf's morning: waking up at 6:00, brushing his teeth, eating breakfast with his family and getting on the yellow school bus"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about present simple affirmative (I play / he plays), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about present simple affirmative (I play / he plays), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows wake up (to stop sleeping); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing wake up: to stop sleeping"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows get dressed (to put on your clothes); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing get dressed: to put on your clothes"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows breakfast (the first meal of the day); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing breakfast: the first meal of the day"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows brush (to clean something with a brush); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing brush: to clean something with a brush"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Four Corners Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Four Corners Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS1-W01","script":"wake up. wake up. I wake up when the sun comes up.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS1-W02","script":"get dressed. get dressed. Rakan gets dressed in five minutes.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS1-W03","script":"breakfast. breakfast. We have eggs and bread for breakfast.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS1-W04","script":"brush. brush. Brush your teeth for two minutes.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS1-T1","script":"Yusuf wakes up at six o'clock every day. He gets dressed and brushes his teeth. Then he has breakfast with his family. His mother makes eggs and bread. Yusuf goes to school by bus. Lessons start at seven. After school, he does his homework and plays football with his cousins. The family eats dinner at eight. Yusuf goes to bed at nine. He loves his busy day!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Yusuf's Busy Day: The Present Simple”. Let’s learn present simple affirmative (I play / he plays) together. Listen to the start of “Yusuf's Busy Day”: Yusuf wakes up at six o'clock every day. He gets dressed and brushes his teeth. Look at the green words. We use the present simple for things we do again and again (routines and habits) and for facts: I get up at six. The sun rises in the east. With he, she, it and one person, add -s to the verb: he plays, she reads, it starts. With I, you, we, they, use the base verb: I play, they read. Here are some examples. I wake up at half past five. My dad drives to work. We pray Fajr with our grandfather. Be careful! Some learners say: “He play football after school.” That’s not right. We say: “He plays football after school.” he/she/it → add -s. Quick check: \"Yusuf goes to bed at nine.\" Does he do this one time or every day? … Think! … Every day – it's a routine. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about my daily routine.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2","title":"What Time Is It? Telling the Time with at, in, on","objectives":["Students will be able to tell the time (o'clock, thirty, fifteen, forty-five).","Students will be able to use at with times, in with parts of the day and on with days.","I can say \"It's seven thirty\".","I can say \"at six o'clock\", \"in the morning\" and \"on Friday\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من قراءة الوقت (o'clock وthirty وfifteen وforty-five).","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام at مع الساعة وin مع أجزاء اليوم وon مع الأيام.","أستطيع أن أقول It's seven thirty.","أستطيع أن أقول at six o'clock وin the morning وon Friday."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"bus","pos":"noun","ipa":"/bʌs/","definition":"a big vehicle that carries many people","arabic":"حافلة","example":"The school bus is yellow.","image_id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS2-W01"},{"word":"lesson","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlɛsən/","definition":"a time when you learn something in class","arabic":"حصة / درس","example":"Our first lesson is math.","image_id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS2-W02"},{"word":"lunch","pos":"noun","ipa":"/lʌntʃ/","definition":"the meal you eat in the middle of the day","arabic":"الغداء","example":"Mom packs sandwiches for lunch.","image_id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS2-W03"},{"word":"homework","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhoʊmˌwɝk/","definition":"school work you do at home","arabic":"واجب منزلي","example":"Saad finishes his homework before dinner.","image_id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"To tell the time, say the hour and the minutes: 7:00 = seven o'clock; 7:30 = seven thirty (or half past seven); 7:15 = seven fifteen (or a quarter after seven); 7:45 = seven forty-five (or a quarter to eight).\nUse at with clock times: at six o'clock. Use in with parts of the day: in the morning, in the afternoon, in the evening (but at night). Use on with days: on Friday, on Monday morning.\nAsk: What time is it? – It's nine o'clock. What time do you…? – I … at …","examples":["It's six o'clock.","School starts at seven fifteen.","We play outside in the afternoon.","My uncle visits us on Thursday evening.","Owls hunt at night.","What time is it? – It's a quarter to nine.","The museum is closed on Sunday.","I read in the evening before bed."],"common_errors":["✗ I wake up in six o'clock. → ✓ I wake up at six o'clock. (Clock times → at.)","✗ We go to the park in Friday. → ✓ We go to the park on Friday. (Days → on.)","✗ I sleep in the night. → ✓ I sleep at night. (We say at night.)","✗ The time is seven. → ✓ It's seven o'clock. (Say It's… for the time.)"],"arabic":"لقراءة الوقت نقول: It's seven o'clock (السابعة تمامًا)، seven thirty (السابعة والنصف).\nat مع الساعة: at six. وin مع أجزاء اليوم: in the morning. وon مع أيام الأسبوع: on Friday.\nانتبه: نقول at night (في الليل) وليس in the night."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “What Time Is It? Telling the Time with at, in, on”. Let’s learn telling the time; prepositions of time at / in / on together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U1-LS2 | What Time Is It? Telling the Time with at, in, on","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: I get up at six o'clock. • We have Arabic in the morning. • They visit Grandpa on Friday. The shop doesn't open at night. • We don't go to school on Saturday. What time is it? – It's eight fifteen. • What time does the lesson start? – At nine.","on_screen":"I get up at six o'clock. • We have Arabic in the morning. • They visit Grandpa on Friday. | The shop doesn't open at night. • We don't go to school on Saturday. | What time is it? – It's eight fifteen. • What time does the lesson start? – At nine.","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"To tell the time, say the hour and the minutes: 7:00 = seven o'clock; 7:30 = seven thirty (or half past seven); 7:15 = seven fifteen (or a quarter after seven); 7:45 = seven forty-five (or a quarter to eight). Use at with clock times: at six o'clock. Use in with parts of the day: in the morning, in the afternoon, in the evening (but at night). Use on with days: on Friday, on Monday morning.","on_screen":"telling the time; prepositions of time at / in / on","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. It's six o'clock. School starts at seven fifteen. We play outside in the afternoon.","on_screen":"It's six o'clock. / School starts at seven fifteen. / We play outside in the afternoon.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I wake up in six o'clock.” That’s not right. We say: “I wake up at six o'clock.” Clock times → at.","on_screen":"✗ I wake up in six o'clock.   ✓ I wake up at six o'clock.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Which word goes with \"Monday\": at, in or on? … Think! … *on* Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"It's seven thirty\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"It's seven thirty\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: telling the time; prepositions of time at / in / on.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","لقراءة الوقت نقول: It's seven o'clock (السابعة تمامًا)، seven thirty (السابعة والنصف).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I wake up in six o'clock. — الصحيح: I wake up at six o'clock.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول It's seven thirty."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"9:00 → It's nine ___.","options":["fifteen","o'clock","half","thirty"],"answer":"o'clock","explanation":"Say the hour, then the minutes: seven thirty, a quarter to eight.","explanation_ar":"الساعة ثم الدقائق."},{"q":"4:30 → It's four ___.","options":["thirty","o'clock","forty","fifteen"],"answer":"thirty","explanation":"Say the hour, then the minutes: seven thirty, a quarter to eight.","explanation_ar":"الساعة ثم الدقائق."},{"q":"The match starts ___ five o'clock.","options":["on","by","in","at"],"answer":"at","explanation":"at + clock time (and at night).","explanation_ar":"at مع الساعة ومع night."},{"q":"I visit my grandparents ___ Friday.","options":["to","on","at","in"],"answer":"on","explanation":"on + days (on Friday, on Monday morning).","explanation_ar":"on مع أيام الأسبوع."},{"q":"We do our homework ___ the afternoon.","options":["at","to","on","in"],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + the morning / the afternoon / the evening.","explanation_ar":"in مع أجزاء اليوم."},{"q":"Bats fly ___ night.","options":["in","the","at","on"],"answer":"at","explanation":"at + clock time (and at night).","explanation_ar":"at مع الساعة ومع night."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the time in words.","items":[{"q":"6:15  (time)","options":[],"answer":"It's six fifteen. / It's a quarter after six.","explanation":"Say the hour, then the minutes: seven thirty, a quarter to eight.","explanation_ar":"الساعة ثم الدقائق."},{"q":"10:45  (time)","options":[],"answer":"It's ten forty-five. / It's a quarter to eleven.","explanation":"Say the hour, then the minutes: seven thirty, a quarter to eight.","explanation_ar":"الساعة ثم الدقائق."},{"q":"1:30  (time)","options":[],"answer":"It's one thirty. / It's half past one.","explanation":"Say the hour, then the minutes: seven thirty, a quarter to eight.","explanation_ar":"الساعة ثم الدقائق."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write at, in or on. Word bank: on, at, in","items":[{"q":"The library closes ______ three thirty.","options":[],"answer":"at","explanation":"at + clock time (and at night).","explanation_ar":"at مع الساعة ومع night."},{"q":"We have art ______ Tuesday.","options":[],"answer":"on","explanation":"on + days (on Friday, on Monday morning).","explanation_ar":"on مع أيام الأسبوع."},{"q":"My dad drinks coffee ______ the morning.","options":[],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + the morning / the afternoon / the evening.","explanation_ar":"in مع أجزاء اليوم."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer about you.","items":[{"q":"What time do you wake up on school days?","options":[],"answer":"I wake up at a quarter to six.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses telling the time; prepositions of time at / in / on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What time does school start?","options":[],"answer":"School starts at seven o'clock.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses telling the time; prepositions of time at / in / on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What do you do in the evening?","options":[],"answer":"In the evening, I read and play with my brother.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses telling the time; prepositions of time at / in / on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What do you do on Friday?","options":[],"answer":"On Friday, I visit my grandparents.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses telling the time; prepositions of time at / in / on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What time is your bedtime?","options":[],"answer":"My bedtime is nine thirty.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses telling the time; prepositions of time at / in / on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Make a timetable.","items":[{"q":"Write your timetable for one school day with 4 times.","options":[],"answer":"6:00 wake up; 6:45 school bus; 12:30 lunch; 9:00 bedtime","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses telling the time; prepositions of time at / in / on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences from your timetable with at, in and on.","options":[],"answer":"I take the bus at six forty-five. I eat lunch at twelve thirty. On Friday, I sleep late.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses telling the time; prepositions of time at / in / on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask a partner \"What time do you…?\" Write his answer.","options":[],"answer":"He has dinner at eight fifteen.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses telling the time; prepositions of time at / in / on correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Snakes & Ladders","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Roll and move. If you land on a cue square, make a sentence with the cue and telling the time; prepositions of time at / in / on.","Correct at the bottom of a ladder: climb. Incorrect at the head of a snake: slide down.","Teammates are the judges and must explain any correction.","First player to reach square 30 wins."],"data":[{"cue":"wake up / 6:00 / he"},{"cue":"have breakfast / 6:30 / we"},{"cue":"the bus / leave / 6:45"},{"cue":"lessons / start / 7:00"},{"cue":"have lunch / 12:00 / she"},{"cue":"do homework / 4:00 / I"},{"cue":"my dad / come home / 5:30"},{"cue":"eat dinner / 8:00 / they"},{"cue":"go to bed / 9:00 / he"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"3:00 → It's three ___.","options":["thirty","quarter","o'clock","half"],"answer":"o'clock","explanation":"Say the hour, then the minutes: seven thirty, a quarter to eight.","explanation_ar":"الساعة ثم الدقائق."},{"q":"7:45 → It's a quarter ___ eight.","options":["at","past","after","to"],"answer":"to","explanation":"Say the hour, then the minutes: seven thirty, a quarter to eight.","explanation_ar":"الساعة ثم الدقائق."},{"q":"The movie begins ___ eight thirty.","options":["at","in","by","on"],"answer":"at","explanation":"at + clock time (and at night).","explanation_ar":"at مع الساعة ومع night."},{"q":"We have P.E. ___ Wednesday.","options":["in","to","on","at"],"answer":"on","explanation":"on + days (on Friday, on Monday morning).","explanation_ar":"on مع أيام الأسبوع."},{"q":"My grandpa walks ___ the evening.","options":["to","in","at","on"],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + the morning / the afternoon / the evening.","explanation_ar":"in مع أجزاء اليوم."},{"q":"","options":["I sleep at the night.","I sleep on night.","I sleep in night.","I sleep at night."],"answer":"I sleep at night.","explanation":"at + clock time (and at night).","explanation_ar":"at مع الساعة ومع night."},{"q":"What time ___? – It's ten fifteen.","options":["it is","it's","is it","time is"],"answer":"is it","explanation":"Say the hour, then the minutes: seven thirty, a quarter to eight.","explanation_ar":"الساعة ثم الدقائق."},{"q":"","options":["The party is in Thursday.","The party is on Thursday.","The party is on the Thursday at.","The party is at Thursday."],"answer":"The party is on Thursday.","explanation":"on + days (on Friday, on Monday morning).","explanation_ar":"on مع أيام الأسبوع."},{"q":"11:30 → It's ___.","options":["half eleven past","eleven three","thirty eleven","eleven thirty"],"answer":"eleven thirty","explanation":"Say the hour, then the minutes: seven thirty, a quarter to eight.","explanation_ar":"الساعة ثم الدقائق."},{"q":"","options":["We pray Asr in the afternoon.","We pray Asr at the afternoon.","We pray Asr on the afternoon.","We pray Asr in afternoon on."],"answer":"We pray Asr in the afternoon.","explanation":"in + the morning / the afternoon / the evening.","explanation_ar":"in مع أجزاء اليوم."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A large classroom clock showing 7:30 next to a weekly timetable, with Sara and Lina pointing at the time. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A large classroom clock showing 7:30 next to a weekly timetable, with Sara and Lina pointing at the time"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of telling the time; prepositions of time at / in / on: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “My Daily Routine”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of telling the time"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows bus (a big vehicle that carries many people); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing bus: a big vehicle that carries many people"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows lesson (a time when you learn something in class); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing lesson: a time when you learn something in class"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows lunch (the meal you eat in the middle of the day); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing lunch: the meal you eat in the middle of the day"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows homework (school work you do at home); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing homework: school work you do at home"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Snakes & Ladders”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Snakes & Ladders"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS2-W01","script":"bus. bus. The school bus is yellow.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS2-W02","script":"lesson. lesson. Our first lesson is math.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS2-W03","script":"lunch. lunch. Mom packs sandwiches for lunch.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS2-W04","script":"homework. homework. Saad finishes his homework before dinner.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “What Time Is It? Telling the Time with at, in, on”. Let’s learn telling the time; prepositions of time at / in / on together. Remember these patterns: I get up at six o'clock. • We have Arabic in the morning. • They visit Grandpa on Friday. The shop doesn't open at night. • We don't go to school on Saturday. What time is it? – It's eight fifteen. • What time does the lesson start? – At nine. To tell the time, say the hour and the minutes: 7:00 = seven o'clock; 7:30 = seven thirty (or half past seven); 7:15 = seven fifteen (or a quarter after seven); 7:45 = seven forty-five (or a quarter to eight). Use at with clock times: at six o'clock. Use in with parts of the day: in the morning, in the afternoon, in the evening (but at night). Use on with days: on Friday, on Monday morning. Here are some examples. It's six o'clock. School starts at seven fifteen. We play outside in the afternoon. Be careful! Some learners say: “I wake up in six o'clock.” That’s not right. We say: “I wake up at six o'clock.” Clock times → at. Quick check: Which word goes with \"Monday\": at, in or on? … Think! … *on* Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"It's seven thirty\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3","title":"Daily Routine Words: Collocations","objectives":["Students will be able to use daily routine phrases with the right verb (have, do, go, get, take, brush).","Students will be able to put routine actions in a logical order.","I can use word partners like \"have breakfast\" and \"do homework\".","I can put my daily activities in order."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام عبارات الروتين اليومي مع الفعل المناسب.","سيتمكن الطلاب من ترتيب أنشطة الروتين ترتيبًا منطقيًا.","أستطيع أن أستخدم الكلمات المترافقة مثل have breakfast وdo homework.","أستطيع أن أرتب أنشطتي اليومية."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"dinner","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdɪnɚ/","definition":"the meal you eat in the evening","arabic":"العشاء","example":"Grandma cooks rice and chicken for dinner.","image_id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS3-W01"},{"word":"early","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈɝli/","definition":"before the usual time","arabic":"مبكرًا","example":"The baker starts work very early.","image_id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS3-W02"},{"word":"late","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/leɪt/","definition":"after the right time","arabic":"متأخرًا","example":"Don't stay up late on school nights.","image_id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS3-W03"},{"word":"bedtime","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbɛdˌtaɪm/","definition":"the time when you go to bed","arabic":"وقت النوم","example":"My bedtime is nine o'clock.","image_id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS3-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Some words like to go together. We call them collocations (word partners): have breakfast, do homework, go to bed.\nLearn the whole phrase, not just one word. In Arabic we say \"أكتب الواجب\" but in English we do homework (NOT make homework).\nSome routine verbs are phrasal verbs (verb + small word): wake up, get up, get dressed.\nCollocations/phrases: have + breakfast / lunch / dinner / a shower | do + homework / the dishes • go + to school / to bed / home | get + up / dressed / ready • brush + your teeth / your hair • take + the bus / a nap","examples":["I have breakfast at six thirty.","My sister does her homework at the kitchen table.","We take the bus to school.","Hamad gets dressed quickly.","The twins go to bed early on school nights.","I brush my hair before school.","Dad has a shower after work.","Don't be late for the bus!"],"common_errors":["✗ I make my homework. → ✓ I do my homework. (homework goes with do.)","✗ I eat my breakfast in six. → ✓ I have breakfast at six. (We usually say have breakfast; clock times → at.)","✗ I go to home. → ✓ I go home. (No to before home.)","✗ I wear my clothes. (for the routine) → ✓ I get dressed. (The routine phrase is get dressed.)"],"arabic":"بعض الكلمات تأتي معًا دائمًا (Collocations): have breakfast وdo homework وgo to bed.\nنقول do homework وليس make homework.\nنقول go home بدون to."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Daily Routine Words: Collocations”. Let’s learn daily routine collocations (have breakfast, brush your teeth, do homework, go to bed) together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U1-LS3 | Daily Routine Words: Collocations","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. dinner: the meal you eat in the evening. early: before the usual time. late: after the right time.","on_screen":"dinner | early | late","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Some words like to go together. We call them collocations (word partners): have breakfast, do homework, go to bed. Learn the whole phrase, not just one word. In Arabic we say \"أكتب الواجب\" but in English we do homework (NOT make homework).","on_screen":"daily routine collocations (have breakfast, brush your teeth, do homework, go to bed)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I have breakfast at six thirty. My sister does her homework at the kitchen table. We take the bus to school.","on_screen":"I have breakfast at six thirty. / My sister does her homework at the kitchen table. / We take the bus to school.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I make my homework.” That’s not right. We say: “I do my homework.” homework goes with do.","on_screen":"✗ I make my homework.   ✓ I do my homework.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Do we say \"make homework\" or \"do homework\"? … Think! … *do homework* Great job! Now you can say: I can use word partners like \"have breakfast\" and \"do homework\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can use word partners like \"have breakfast\" and \"do homework\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: daily routine collocations (have breakfast, brush your teeth, do homework, go to bed).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","بعض الكلمات تأتي معًا دائمًا (Collocations): have breakfast وdo homework وgo to bed.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I make my homework. — الصحيح: I do my homework.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أستخدم الكلمات المترافقة مثل have breakfast وdo homework."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"I ___ breakfast with my family.","options":["have","go","do","make"],"answer":"have","explanation":"Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Majed ___ his homework in his room.","options":["makes","does","goes","has"],"answer":"does","explanation":"Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"We ___ the bus at a quarter to seven.","options":["make","take","do","have"],"answer":"take","explanation":"Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Please ___ your teeth after meals.","options":["take","wash","do","brush"],"answer":"brush","explanation":"Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"After school, I go ___.","options":["at home","in home","to home","home"],"answer":"home","explanation":"go home – no to.","explanation_ar":"نقول go home بدون to."},{"q":"The bus leaves at 6:30. I arrive at 6:40. I am ___.","options":["on time","early","late","ready"],"answer":"late","explanation":"early = before the usual time; late = after the right time.","explanation_ar":"early مبكرًا وlate متأخرًا."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Number the activities in the right order (1–6).","items":[{"q":"wake up","options":["1","3","4","6","2","5"],"answer":"1","explanation":"wake up → 1. Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"get dressed","options":["1","3","4","6","2","5"],"answer":"2","explanation":"get dressed → 2. Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"have breakfast","options":["1","3","4","6","2","5"],"answer":"3","explanation":"have breakfast → 3. Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"go to school","options":["1","3","4","6","2","5"],"answer":"4","explanation":"go to school → 4. Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"do homework","options":["1","3","4","6","2","5"],"answer":"5","explanation":"do homework → 5. Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"go to bed","options":["1","3","4","6","2","5"],"answer":"6","explanation":"go to bed → 6. Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Complete with your own routine.","items":[{"q":"I have breakfast at ___.","options":[],"answer":"I have breakfast at six fifteen.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses daily routine collocations (have breakfast, brush your teeth, do homework, go to bed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I do my homework in the ___.","options":[],"answer":"I do my homework in the living room.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses daily routine collocations (have breakfast, brush your teeth, do homework, go to bed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I go to bed at ___ on school nights.","options":[],"answer":"I go to bed at nine o'clock on school nights.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses daily routine collocations (have breakfast, brush your teeth, do homework, go to bed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I brush my teeth ___ times a day.","options":[],"answer":"I brush my teeth two times a day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses daily routine collocations (have breakfast, brush your teeth, do homework, go to bed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I take ___ to school.","options":[],"answer":"I take the school bus to school.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses daily routine collocations (have breakfast, brush your teeth, do homework, go to bed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Make a routine wheel.","items":[{"q":"Draw a routine wheel with 6 activities and times.","options":[],"answer":"5:30 wake up, 6:00 have breakfast, 6:30 take the bus, 3:00 do homework, 8:00 have dinner, 9:00 go to bed","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses daily routine collocations (have breakfast, brush your teeth, do homework, go to bed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 4 sentences about your weekend routine.","options":[],"answer":"I wake up late. I have a big breakfast. I visit my cousins. I go to bed at ten.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses daily routine collocations (have breakfast, brush your teeth, do homework, go to bed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about someone who is always late.","options":[],"answer":"He gets up late. He misses the bus.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses daily routine collocations (have breakfast, brush your teeth, do homework, go to bed) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Dominoes","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Deal the dominoes equally in teams of four.","Player 1 places a domino; the next player adds a domino whose word matches the open definition.","If you cannot play, pass.","The first player with no dominoes left wins."],"data":[{"word":"wake up","match":"to stop sleeping","arabic":"يستيقظ"},{"word":"get dressed","match":"to put on your clothes","arabic":"يرتدي ملابسه"},{"word":"breakfast","match":"the first meal of the day","arabic":"الفطور"},{"word":"brush","match":"to clean something with a brush","arabic":"يُنظّف بالفرشاة"},{"word":"bus","match":"a big vehicle that carries many people","arabic":"حافلة"},{"word":"lesson","match":"a time when you learn something in class","arabic":"حصة / درس"},{"word":"lunch","match":"the meal you eat in the middle of the day","arabic":"الغداء"},{"word":"homework","match":"school work you do at home","arabic":"واجب منزلي"},{"word":"dinner","match":"the meal you eat in the evening","arabic":"العشاء"},{"word":"early","match":"before the usual time","arabic":"مبكرًا"},{"word":"late","match":"after the right time","arabic":"متأخرًا"},{"word":"bedtime","match":"the time when you go to bed","arabic":"وقت النوم"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"We ___ dinner at eight.","options":["have","go","do","make"],"answer":"have","explanation":"Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Please ___ the dishes after dinner.","options":["make","have","do","take"],"answer":"do","explanation":"Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"I ___ up at six.","options":["take","do","have","get"],"answer":"get","explanation":"Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"","options":["I go home at two.","I go in home at two.","I go at home at two.","I go to home at two."],"answer":"I go home at two.","explanation":"go home – no to.","explanation_ar":"نقول go home بدون to."},{"q":"My dad ___ a nap after lunch.","options":["takes","makes","goes","does"],"answer":"takes","explanation":"Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Which comes first in the morning?","options":["have dinner","go to bed","do homework","wake up"],"answer":"wake up","explanation":"Think about the logical order of the day.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في الترتيب المنطقي لليوم."},{"q":"The test starts at 8:00. Ali arrives at 7:30. He is ___.","options":["late","tired","early","sleepy"],"answer":"early","explanation":"early = before the usual time; late = after the right time.","explanation_ar":"early مبكرًا وlate متأخرًا."},{"q":"","options":["My cousin makes his homework after Asr.","My cousin goes his homework after Asr.","My cousin does his homework after Asr.","My cousin has his homework after Asr."],"answer":"My cousin does his homework after Asr.","explanation":"Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"I ___ my hair every morning.","options":["go","brush","make","do"],"answer":"brush","explanation":"Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Which comes last at night?","options":["have breakfast","go to bed","get dressed","take the bus"],"answer":"go to bed","explanation":"Think about the logical order of the day.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في الترتيب المنطقي لليوم."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A circular routine wheel with small pictures: wake up, get dressed, have breakfast, go to school, do homework, have dinner, brush teeth, go to bed. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A circular routine wheel with small pictures: wake up, get dressed, have breakfast, go to school, do homework, have dinner, brush teeth, go to bed"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows dinner (the meal you eat in the evening); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing dinner: the meal you eat in the evening"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows early (before the usual time); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing early: before the usual time"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows late (after the right time); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing late: after the right time"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows bedtime (the time when you go to bed); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing bedtime: the time when you go to bed"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Dominoes”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Dominoes"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS3-W01","script":"dinner. dinner. Grandma cooks rice and chicken for dinner.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS3-W02","script":"early. early. The baker starts work very early.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS3-W03","script":"late. late. Don't stay up late on school nights.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS3-W04","script":"bedtime. bedtime. My bedtime is nine o'clock.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Daily Routine Words: Collocations”. Let’s learn daily routine collocations (have breakfast, brush your teeth, do homework, go to bed) together. Meet some new words. dinner: the meal you eat in the evening. early: before the usual time. late: after the right time. Some words like to go together. We call them collocations (word partners): have breakfast, do homework, go to bed. Learn the whole phrase, not just one word. In Arabic we say \"أكتب الواجب\" but in English we do homework (NOT make homework). Here are some examples. I have breakfast at six thirty. My sister does her homework at the kitchen table. We take the bus to school. Be careful! Some learners say: “I make my homework.” That’s not right. We say: “I do my homework.” homework goes with do. Quick check: Do we say \"make homework\" or \"do homework\"? … Think! … *do homework* Great job! Now you can say: I can use word partners like \"have breakfast\" and \"do homework\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS4","title":"Plays, Watches, Studies: Spelling Verbs with -s","objectives":["Students will be able to spell he/she/it verbs with -s, -es and -ies.","Students will be able to correct spelling mistakes in a short paragraph.","I can spell \"watches\", \"studies\" and \"plays\".","I can fix spelling mistakes in verbs."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تهجئة الأفعال مع he/she/it بإضافة s وes وies.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تصحيح أخطاء التهجئة في فقرة قصيرة.","أستطيع أن أتهجّى watches وstudies وplays.","أستطيع أن أصحح أخطاء تهجئة الأفعال."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"wake up","pos":"phrasal verb","ipa":"/weɪk ʌp/","definition":"to stop sleeping","arabic":"يستيقظ","example":"I wake up when the sun comes up.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"get dressed","pos":"verb phrase","ipa":"/ɡɛt drɛst/","definition":"to put on your clothes","arabic":"يرتدي ملابسه","example":"Rakan gets dressed in five minutes.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"breakfast","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbrɛkfəst/","definition":"the first meal of the day","arabic":"الفطور","example":"We have eggs and bread for breakfast.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"brush","pos":"verb","ipa":"/brʌʃ/","definition":"to clean something with a brush","arabic":"يُنظّف بالفرشاة","example":"Brush your teeth for two minutes.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bus","pos":"noun","ipa":"/bʌs/","definition":"a big vehicle that carries many people","arabic":"حافلة","example":"The school bus is yellow.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"lesson","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlɛsən/","definition":"a time when you learn something in class","arabic":"حصة / درس","example":"Our first lesson is math.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Most verbs add -s: play → plays, read → reads.\nVerbs ending in s, ss, sh, ch, x, o add -es: wash → washes, watch → watches, fix → fixes, go → goes.\nVerbs ending in consonant + y change y → ies: study → studies, cry → cries. But vowel + y adds -s: play → plays.\n+ s: walks, eats, reads, plays\n+ es after s, ss, sh, ch, x, o: kisses, brushes, catches, fixes, goes, does\nconsonant + y → ies: studies, tries, flies\nspecial: have → has","examples":["My brother studies at the library.","She fixes her bike in the garage.","The baby cries when he is hungry.","Grandpa washes his car on Friday.","Dad goes to work early.","The plane flies to Riyadh.","Lina plays with her cat.","The teacher teaches us English."],"common_errors":["✗ He studys hard. → ✓ He studies hard. (consonant + y → ies.)","✗ She watchs TV. → ✓ She watches TV. (after ch → -es.)","✗ He plaies football. → ✓ He plays football. (vowel + y → just -s.)","✗ She gos to school. → ✓ She goes to school. (go → goes.)"],"arabic":"معظم الأفعال نضيف لها s: plays.\nالأفعال المنتهية بـ s وsh وch وx وo نضيف لها es: watches, goes.\nإذا انتهى الفعل بحرف ساكن + y نحذف y ونضيف ies: studies، أما المتحرك + y فنضيف s فقط: plays."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Plays, Watches, Studies: Spelling Verbs with -s”. Let’s learn spelling present simple verbs with -s, -es, -ies together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U1-LS4 | Plays, Watches, Studies: Spelling Verbs with -s","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Most verbs add -s: play → plays, read → reads.","on_screen":"spelling present simple verbs with -s, -es, -ies","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Most verbs add -s: play → plays, read → reads. Verbs ending in s, ss, sh, ch, x, o add -es: wash → washes, watch → watches, fix → fixes, go → goes.","on_screen":"+ s: walks, eats, reads, plays • + es after s, ss, sh, ch, x, o: kisses, brushes, catches, fixes, goes, does • consonant + y → ies: studies, tries, flies","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My brother studies at the library. She fixes her bike in the garage. The baby cries when he is hungry.","on_screen":"My brother studies at the library. / She fixes her bike in the garage. / The baby cries when he is hungry.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “He studys hard.” That’s not right. We say: “He studies hard.” consonant + y → ies.","on_screen":"✗ He studys hard.   ✓ He studies hard.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Is it \"plaies\" or \"plays\"? Why? … Think! … *plays* – a vowel (a) comes before y. Great job! Now you can say: I can spell \"watches\", \"studies\" and \"plays\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can spell \"watches\", \"studies\" and \"plays\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: spelling present simple verbs with -s, -es, -ies.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","معظم الأفعال نضيف لها s: plays.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: He studys hard. — الصحيح: He studies hard.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتهجّى watches وstudies وplays."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Rakan's Morning (editing passage)","body":"Rakan wake up at six. He brushs his teeth and gets dressed. His sister studys in the morning. Rakan watchs the news with his dad. Then he gos to school.","word_count":30,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct spelling.","items":[{"q":"She ___ her face. (wash)","options":["washs","washe","washes","washies"],"answer":"washes","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch, x, o: add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx وo نضيف es."},{"q":"He ___ hard for tests. (study)","options":["studis","studys","studies","studyes"],"answer":"studies","explanation":"Consonant + y → ies.","explanation_ar":"حرف ساكن + y ← ies."},{"q":"The bird ___ high. (fly)","options":["flies","flyes","flis","flys"],"answer":"flies","explanation":"Consonant + y → ies.","explanation_ar":"حرف ساكن + y ← ies."},{"q":"My cousin ___ video games. (play)","options":["plaies","plays","plais","playes"],"answer":"plays","explanation":"Vowel + y → add -s only.","explanation_ar":"حرف متحرك + y ← s فقط."},{"q":"Mom ___ dinner at seven. (cook)","options":["cooks's","cookies","cookes","cooks"],"answer":"cooks","explanation":"Most verbs: add -s.","explanation_ar":"معظم الأفعال: نضيف s."},{"q":"Dad ___ to the mosque early. (go)","options":["goes","gos","gose","goies"],"answer":"goes","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch, x, o: add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx وo نضيف es."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the spelling mistake.","items":[{"q":"My uncle fixs old cars.","options":[],"answer":"My uncle fixes old cars.","explanation":"fixs → fixes. After s, ss, sh, ch, x, o: add -es.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: fixs → fixes. بعد s وsh وch وx وo نضيف es."},{"q":"The boy trys again and again.","options":[],"answer":"The boy tries again and again.","explanation":"trys → tries. Consonant + y → ies.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: trys → tries. حرف ساكن + y ← ies."},{"q":"Noura enjoies her art class.","options":[],"answer":"Noura enjoys her art class.","explanation":"enjoies → enjoys. Vowel + y → add -s only.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: enjoies → enjoys. حرف متحرك + y ← s فقط."},{"q":"Dad haves coffee at ten.","options":[],"answer":"Dad has coffee at ten.","explanation":"haves → has. have → has.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: haves → has. have تصبح has."},{"q":"The baby kisss her mother.","options":[],"answer":"The baby kisses her mother.","explanation":"kisss → kisses. After s, ss, sh, ch, x, o: add -es.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: kisss → kisses. بعد s وsh وch وx وo نضيف es."},{"q":"Our coach catchs the ball.","options":[],"answer":"Our coach catches the ball.","explanation":"catchs → catches. After s, ss, sh, ch, x, o: add -es.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: catchs → catches. بعد s وsh وch وx وo نضيف es."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit Rakan's paragraph.","items":[{"q":"Rakan wake up at six.","options":[],"answer":"Rakan wakes up at six.","explanation":"wake → wakes. Most verbs: add -s.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: wake → wakes. معظم الأفعال: نضيف s."},{"q":"He brushs his teeth and gets dressed.","options":[],"answer":"He brushes his teeth and gets dressed.","explanation":"brushs → brushes. Most verbs: add -s.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: brushs → brushes. معظم الأفعال: نضيف s."},{"q":"His sister studys in the morning.","options":[],"answer":"His sister studies in the morning.","explanation":"studys → studies. Most verbs: add -s.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: studys → studies. معظم الأفعال: نضيف s."},{"q":"Rakan watchs the news with his dad.","options":[],"answer":"Rakan watches the news with his dad.","explanation":"watchs → watches. Most verbs: add -s.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: watchs → watches. معظم الأفعال: نضيف s."},{"q":"Then he gos to school.","options":[],"answer":"Then he goes to school.","explanation":"gos → goes. Most verbs: add -s.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: gos → goes. معظم الأفعال: نضيف s."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write about a family member.","items":[{"q":"Write 4 sentences about one person in your family. Use -s, -es or -ies verbs.","options":[],"answer":"My sister studies every day. She watches cartoons. She plays with dolls. She goes to bed at eight.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses spelling present simple verbs with -s, -es, -ies correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 verbs that end in -ies with he/she.","options":[],"answer":"tries, cries, carries","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses spelling present simple verbs with -s, -es, -ies correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Swap with a partner. Check the spelling of his verbs. Write one correction.","options":[],"answer":"\"catchs\" → \"catches\"","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses spelling present simple verbs with -s, -es, -ies correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Speed Spell","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a word and a short sentence with it.","Students write the word in 10 seconds.","Show boards on \"Show me!\". Correct = 1 point.","After 10 words, partners check each other's boards and correct any mistakes."],"data":[{"word":"wakes","clue":""},{"word":"brushes","clue":""},{"word":"watches","clue":""},{"word":"studies","clue":""},{"word":"goes","clue":""},{"word":"does","clue":""},{"word":"plays","clue":""},{"word":"flies","clue":""},{"word":"fixes","clue":""},{"word":"has","clue":""},{"word":"breakfast","clue":"the first meal of the day"},{"word":"brush","clue":"to clean something with a brush"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"He ___ the window. (close)","options":["closses","closs","closies","closes"],"answer":"closes","explanation":"Most verbs: add -s.","explanation_ar":"معظم الأفعال: نضيف s."},{"q":"She ___ the baby. (carry)","options":["carryes","carris","carries","carrys"],"answer":"carries","explanation":"Consonant + y → ies.","explanation_ar":"حرف ساكن + y ← ies."},{"q":"The cat ___ mice. (catch)","options":["catche","catchs","catchies","catches"],"answer":"catches","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch, x, o: add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx وo نضيف es."},{"q":"My dad ___ a new car. (buy)","options":["buies","buys","buis","buyes"],"answer":"buys","explanation":"Vowel + y → add -s only.","explanation_ar":"حرف متحرك + y ← s فقط."},{"q":"Grandma ___ the plants. (water)","options":["waters'","wateries","waters","wateres"],"answer":"waters","explanation":"Most verbs: add -s.","explanation_ar":"معظم الأفعال: نضيف s."},{"q":"","options":["The teacher teachs us math.","The teacher teachies us math.","The teacher teaches us math.","The teacher teache us math."],"answer":"The teacher teaches us math.","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch, x, o: add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx وo نضيف es."},{"q":"Which spelling is correct?","options":["does","dos","doese","doies"],"answer":"does","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch, x, o: add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx وo نضيف es."},{"q":"","options":["My brother worryes about tests.","My brother worrys about tests.","My brother worris about tests.","My brother worries about tests."],"answer":"My brother worries about tests.","explanation":"Consonant + y → ies.","explanation_ar":"حرف ساكن + y ← ies."},{"q":"She ___ her room on Saturday. (tidy)","options":["tidies","tidys","tidyes","tidis"],"answer":"tidies","explanation":"Consonant + y → ies.","explanation_ar":"حرف ساكن + y ← ies."},{"q":"The robot ___ dishes! (wash)","options":["washies","washes","washs","wash"],"answer":"washes","explanation":"After s, ss, sh, ch, x, o: add -es.","explanation_ar":"بعد s وsh وch وx وo نضيف es."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “My Daily Routine” that shows spelling present simple verbs with -s, -es, -ies in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “My Daily Routine” that shows spelling present simple verbs with -s, -es, -ies in action"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Speed Spell”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Speed Spell"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Plays, Watches, Studies: Spelling Verbs with -s”. Let’s learn spelling present simple verbs with -s, -es, -ies together. Most verbs add -s: play → plays, read → reads. Most verbs add -s: play → plays, read → reads. Verbs ending in s, ss, sh, ch, x, o add -es: wash → washes, watch → watches, fix → fixes, go → goes. Here are some examples. My brother studies at the library. She fixes her bike in the garage. The baby cries when he is hungry. Be careful! Some learners say: “He studys hard.” That’s not right. We say: “He studies hard.” consonant + y → ies. Quick check: Is it \"plaies\" or \"plays\"? Why? … Think! … *plays* – a vowel (a) comes before y. Great job! Now you can say: I can spell \"watches\", \"studies\" and \"plays\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS5","title":"A Day in My Life: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to describe their daily routine in speech and writing.","Students will be able to write a \"Day in My Life\" paragraph with times and correct verb forms.","I can tell my partner about my day.","I can write a paragraph about my day."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف روتينهم اليومي تحدثًا وكتابة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة فقرة «يوم في حياتي» مع الأوقات وصيغ الأفعال الصحيحة.","أستطيع أن أخبر زميلي عن يومي.","أستطيع أن أكتب فقرة عن يومي."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"wake up","pos":"phrasal verb","ipa":"/weɪk ʌp/","definition":"to stop sleeping","arabic":"يستيقظ","example":"I wake up when the sun comes up.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"get dressed","pos":"verb phrase","ipa":"/ɡɛt drɛst/","definition":"to put on your clothes","arabic":"يرتدي ملابسه","example":"Rakan gets dressed in five minutes.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"breakfast","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbrɛkfəst/","definition":"the first meal of the day","arabic":"الفطور","example":"We have eggs and bread for breakfast.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"brush","pos":"verb","ipa":"/brʌʃ/","definition":"to clean something with a brush","arabic":"يُنظّف بالفرشاة","example":"Brush your teeth for two minutes.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bus","pos":"noun","ipa":"/bʌs/","definition":"a big vehicle that carries many people","arabic":"حافلة","example":"The school bus is yellow.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"lesson","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlɛsən/","definition":"a time when you learn something in class","arabic":"حصة / درس","example":"Our first lesson is math.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"lunch","pos":"noun","ipa":"/lʌntʃ/","definition":"the meal you eat in the middle of the day","arabic":"الغداء","example":"Mom packs sandwiches for lunch.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"homework","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhoʊmˌwɝk/","definition":"school work you do at home","arabic":"واجب منزلي","example":"Saad finishes his homework before dinner.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"dinner","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdɪnɚ/","definition":"the meal you eat in the evening","arabic":"العشاء","example":"Grandma cooks rice and chicken for dinner.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"early","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈɝli/","definition":"before the usual time","arabic":"مبكرًا","example":"The baker starts work very early.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"late","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/leɪt/","definition":"after the right time","arabic":"متأخرًا","example":"Don't stay up late on school nights.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bedtime","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbɛdˌtaɪm/","definition":"the time when you go to bed","arabic":"وقت النوم","example":"My bedtime is nine o'clock.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 1: the present simple, at/in/on with times, routine word partners and verb spelling.\nGood routine writing follows the order of the day and uses time words: first, then, after that, in the afternoon, at night.\n✔ present simple: I get up / he gets up\n✔ times: at six, in the morning, on Friday\n✔ word partners: have breakfast, do homework, go to bed\n✔ order words: first, then, after that","examples":["First, I have a shower.","Then I get dressed.","My mom makes sandwiches in the morning.","After that, we take the bus.","My little brother watches cartoons at four.","We visit our grandparents on Friday.","My dad finishes work at five.","I read a book at night."],"common_errors":["✗ In the morning, I am wake up at six. → ✓ In the morning, I wake up at six. (No am before a present simple verb.)","✗ My brother go to bed early. → ✓ My brother goes to bed early. (he → goes.)","✗ I make my homework in four. → ✓ I do my homework at four. (do homework; at + clock time.)"],"arabic":"نراجع المضارع البسيط وحروف الوقت والكلمات المترافقة وتهجئة الأفعال.\nاكتب الأحداث بالترتيب واستخدم first وthen وafter that.\nتذكّر s مع he وshe وit، وat مع الساعة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Day in My Life: Language in Use”. Let’s learn present simple, time phrases, routine collocations and verb spelling (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U1-LS5 | A Day in My Life: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Routine interview: ask a partner \"What time do you get up? What do you have for breakfast? What do you do after school?\" Then tell the class about your partner's day with he.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 1: the present simple, at/in/on with times, routine word partners and verb spelling. Good routine writing follows the order of the day and uses time words: first, then, after that, in the afternoon, at night.","on_screen":"✔ present simple: I get up / he gets up • ✔ times: at six, in the morning, on Friday • ✔ word partners: have breakfast, do homework, go to bed","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. First, I have a shower. Then I get dressed. My mom makes sandwiches in the morning.","on_screen":"First, I have a shower. / Then I get dressed. / My mom makes sandwiches in the morning.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “In the morning, I am wake up at six.” That’s not right. We say: “In the morning, I wake up at six.” No am before a present simple verb.","on_screen":"✗ In the morning, I am wake up at six.   ✓ In the morning, I wake up at six.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “My brother go to bed early.”? … Think! … It should be “My brother goes to bed early.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can tell my partner about my day.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can tell my partner about my day.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present simple, time phrases, routine collocations and verb spelling (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع المضارع البسيط وحروف الوقت والكلمات المترافقة وتهجئة الأفعال.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: In the morning, I am wake up at six. — الصحيح: In the morning, I wake up at six.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أخبر زميلي عن يومي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"A Day in My Life – Adam","body":"I wake up at six o'clock. I get dressed and have breakfast with my brother.\nMy dad drives us to school at a quarter to seven.\nIn the afternoon, I do my homework and play with my robot kit.\nWe have dinner at eight thirty.\nI go to bed at nine thirty. My day is busy but fun!","word_count":58,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Adam's text. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Adam wakes up at six o'clock.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Day in My Life – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam goes to school by bus.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “A Day in My Life – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"He does his homework in the afternoon.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Day in My Life – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"They have dinner at seven thirty.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “A Day in My Life – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam plays with a robot kit.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Day in My Life – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam thinks his day is boring.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “A Day in My Life – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Adam's dad ___ them to school.","options":["driving","drives","is drive","drive"],"answer":"drives","explanation":"Present simple: base verb with I/you/we/they; -s with he/she/it.","explanation_ar":"المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"They have dinner ___ eight thirty.","options":["on","in","at","to"],"answer":"at","explanation":"at + time; in + part of the day; on + day.","explanation_ar":"at للساعة وin لأجزاء اليوم وon للأيام."},{"q":"Adam ___ his homework in the afternoon.","options":["does","takes","makes","has"],"answer":"does","explanation":"Use the right word partner.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"My aunt ___ English at a school. (teach)","options":["teachs","teache","teachies","teaches"],"answer":"teaches","explanation":"Check the -s/-es/-ies spelling.","explanation_ar":"تحقق من تهجئة الفعل."},{"q":"___, I wake up. Then I get dressed.","options":["Night","Late","First","Last"],"answer":"First","explanation":"Use order words: first, then, after that.","explanation_ar":"استخدم كلمات الترتيب."},{"q":"We visit the museum ___ Saturday.","options":["at","on","to","in"],"answer":"on","explanation":"at + time; in + part of the day; on + day.","explanation_ar":"at للساعة وin لأجزاء اليوم وon للأيام."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Interview a partner. Write his answers with he.","items":[{"q":"What time does he get up?","options":[],"answer":"He gets up at five forty-five.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple, time phrases, routine collocations and verb spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What does he have for breakfast?","options":[],"answer":"He has bread and honey.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple, time phrases, routine collocations and verb spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How does he go to school?","options":[],"answer":"He goes to school by car.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple, time phrases, routine collocations and verb spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What does he do in the afternoon?","options":[],"answer":"He plays football with his brothers.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple, time phrases, routine collocations and verb spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What time does he go to bed?","options":[],"answer":"He goes to bed at nine.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple, time phrases, routine collocations and verb spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write \"A Day in My Life\".","items":[{"q":"Plan: write 6 activities with times in order.","options":[],"answer":"6:00 wake up; 6:20 breakfast; 6:45 bus; 2:00 lunch; 4:00 homework; 9:00 bed","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple, time phrases, routine collocations and verb spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 5–6 sentences. Use first, then and after that.","options":[],"answer":"First, I wake up at six. Then I have breakfast. After that, I take the bus at a quarter to seven. In the afternoon, I do my homework. I go to bed at nine.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple, time phrases, routine collocations and verb spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: -s with he/she? at/in/on? word partners? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"make homework\" to \"do homework\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple, time phrases, routine collocations and verb spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin the Review Wheel","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["A player spins the wheel and lands on a word.","Say what the word means and use it in a sentence with present simple, time phrases, routine collocations and verb spelling (unit review).","Teammates check: meaning (1 point), grammar (1 point), pronunciation (1 point).","Highest total after 6 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"wake up","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"get dressed","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"breakfast","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"brush","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"bus","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"lesson","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"lunch","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"homework","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"dinner","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"early","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"late","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"bedtime","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"My grandma ___ bread every morning. (bake)","options":["bake","bakes","is bake","bakies"],"answer":"bakes","explanation":"Present simple: base verb with I/you/we/they; -s with he/she/it.","explanation_ar":"المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"The library opens ___ eight o'clock.","options":["in","at","on","to"],"answer":"at","explanation":"at + time; in + part of the day; on + day.","explanation_ar":"at للساعة وin لأجزاء اليوم وon للأيام."},{"q":"I ___ a shower after football.","options":["go","make","do","have"],"answer":"have","explanation":"Use the right word partner.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The baby ___ a lot at night. (cry)","options":["cry","crys","cries","cryes"],"answer":"cries","explanation":"Check the -s/-es/-ies spelling.","explanation_ar":"تحقق من تهجئة الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["First, I get up. Then I pray.","First I get up then. I pray.","First, I gets up. Then I prays.","First, I am get up. Then I pray."],"answer":"First, I get up. Then I pray.","explanation":"Use order words: first, then, after that.","explanation_ar":"استخدم كلمات الترتيب."},{"q":"We go to the farm ___ Friday morning.","options":["in","at","to","on"],"answer":"on","explanation":"at + time; in + part of the day; on + day.","explanation_ar":"at للساعة وin لأجزاء اليوم وon للأيام."},{"q":"","options":["My friends plays football after school.","My friends play football after school.","My friends playing football after school.","My friends is play football after school."],"answer":"My friends play football after school.","explanation":"Present simple: base verb with I/you/we/they; -s with he/she/it.","explanation_ar":"المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"I always ___ my bed.","options":["take","have","make","do"],"answer":"make","explanation":"Use the right word partner.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Lessons finish ___ the afternoon.","options":["in","at","on","to"],"answer":"in","explanation":"at + time; in + part of the day; on + day.","explanation_ar":"at للساعة وin لأجزاء اليوم وon للأيام."},{"q":"","options":["He makes his homework and goes to bed.","He does his homework and gos to bed.","He does his homework and goes to bed.","He do his homework and go to bed."],"answer":"He does his homework and goes to bed.","explanation":"Check the -s/-es/-ies spelling.","explanation_ar":"تحقق من تهجئة الفعل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Adam presenting a \"Day in My Life\" timeline poster with clock pictures from morning to night. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Adam presenting a \"Day in My Life\" timeline poster with clock pictures from morning to night"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “My Daily Routine”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “My Daily Routine”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L02-U1-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin the Review Wheel”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin the Review Wheel"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS5-T1","script":"I wake up at six o'clock. I get dressed and have breakfast with my brother. My dad drives us to school at a quarter to seven. In the afternoon, I do my homework and play with my robot kit. We have dinner at eight thirty. I go to bed at nine thirty. My day is busy but fun!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U1-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Day in My Life: Language in Use”. Let’s learn present simple, time phrases, routine collocations and verb spelling (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Routine interview: ask a partner \"What time do you get up? What do you have for breakfast? What do you do after school?\" Then tell the class about your partner's day with he. Today you use all of Unit 1: the present simple, at/in/on with times, routine word partners and verb spelling. Good routine writing follows the order of the day and uses time words: first, then, after that, in the afternoon, at night. Here are some examples. First, I have a shower. Then I get dressed. My mom makes sandwiches in the morning. Be careful! Some learners say: “In the morning, I am wake up at six.” That’s not right. We say: “In the morning, I wake up at six.” No am before a present simple verb. Quick check: what is wrong with “My brother go to bed early.”? … Think! … It should be “My brother goes to bed early.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can tell my partner about my day.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"My brother ___ to school by bus.","options":["going","goes","go","is go"],"answer":"goes","explanation":"Verbs ending in o, sh, ch, x → add -es (goes, watches).","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المنتهية بـ o وsh وch وx تأخذ es."},{"q":"We ___ breakfast at six thirty.","options":["having","have","has","haves"],"answer":"have","explanation":"I / you / we / they → base verb (no -s).","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey الفعل بدون s."},{"q":"The train ___ at ten.","options":["leaves","leave","leaving","is leave"],"answer":"leaves","explanation":"he / she / it → verb + -s.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نضيف s للفعل."},{"q":"My uncle ___ a big farm.","options":["haves","is have","have","has"],"answer":"has","explanation":"he / she / it → has (not haves).","explanation_ar":"have تصبح has مع المفرد الغائب."},{"q":"","options":["Sara read a book every night.","Sara reading a book every night.","Sara reads a book every night.","Sara is read a book every night."],"answer":"Sara reads a book every night.","explanation":"Don't use am/is/are before a present simple verb.","explanation_ar":"لا نضع is قبل فعل المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"5:30 → It's five ___.","options":["o'clock","thirty","fifteen","quarter"],"answer":"thirty","explanation":"Say the hour, then the minutes: seven thirty, a quarter to eight.","explanation_ar":"الساعة ثم الدقائق."},{"q":"2:45 → It's a quarter ___ three.","options":["past","at","to","after"],"answer":"to","explanation":"Say the hour, then the minutes: seven thirty, a quarter to eight.","explanation_ar":"الساعة ثم الدقائق."},{"q":"We have science ___ Monday.","options":["to","in","at","on"],"answer":"on","explanation":"on + days (on Friday, on Monday morning).","explanation_ar":"on مع أيام الأسبوع."},{"q":"I drink milk ___ the morning.","options":["in","on","to","at"],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + the morning / the afternoon / the evening.","explanation_ar":"in مع أجزاء اليوم."},{"q":"","options":["Cats see well at the night.","Cats see well in night.","Cats see well on night.","Cats see well at night."],"answer":"Cats see well at night.","explanation":"at + clock time (and at night).","explanation_ar":"at مع الساعة ومع night."},{"q":"I ___ my homework after lunch.","options":["make","have","take","do"],"answer":"do","explanation":"Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"We ___ dinner together.","options":["do","have","make","go"],"answer":"have","explanation":"Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"","options":["I go to home at three.","I go in home at three.","I go home at three.","I go at home at three."],"answer":"I go home at three.","explanation":"go home – no to.","explanation_ar":"نقول go home بدون to."},{"q":"I ___ the school bus every day.","options":["have","do","make","take"],"answer":"take","explanation":"Use the right word partner (collocation).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الكلمة المرافقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Which comes first?","options":["get dressed","do homework","go to bed","have dinner"],"answer":"get dressed","explanation":"Think about the logical order of the day.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في الترتيب المنطقي لليوم."},{"q":"The bus comes at 7:00. Fahad arrives at 7:10. He is ___.","options":["late","early","ready","on time"],"answer":"late","explanation":"Say the hour, then the minutes: seven thirty, a quarter to eight.","explanation_ar":"الساعة ثم الدقائق."},{"q":"She ___ her bike. (fix)","options":["fixe","fixies","fixs","fixes"],"answer":"fixes","explanation":"Verbs ending in o, sh, ch, x → add -es (goes, watches).","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المنتهية بـ o وsh وch وx تأخذ es."},{"q":"My sister ___ hard. (study)","options":["studis","studies","studys","studyes"],"answer":"studies","explanation":"Consonant + y → ies.","explanation_ar":"حرف ساكن + y ← ies."},{"q":"He ___ football every day. (play)","options":["plaies","playes","plays","plais"],"answer":"plays","explanation":"Vowel + y → add -s only.","explanation_ar":"حرف متحرك + y ← s فقط."},{"q":"","options":["Grandpa watches the news.","Grandpa watchies the news.","Grandpa watchs the news.","Grandpa watche the news."],"answer":"Grandpa watches the news.","explanation":"Verbs ending in o, sh, ch, x → add -es (goes, watches).","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المنتهية بـ o وsh وch وx تأخذ es."},{"q":"","options":["goes","gos","goies","gose"],"answer":"goes","explanation":"Verbs ending in o, sh, ch, x → add -es (goes, watches).","explanation_ar":"الأفعال المنتهية بـ o وsh وch وx تأخذ es."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for \"A Day in My Life\":","options":["I am have breakfast at six fifteen.","I make breakfast in six fifteen.","I have breakfast at six fifteen.","I has breakfast at six fifteen."],"answer":"I have breakfast at six fifteen.","explanation":"Present simple: base verb with I/you/we/they; -s with he/she/it.","explanation_ar":"المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"my sister wake up in six.\"","options":["my sister wakes up at six.","My sister wakes up at six.","My sister wake up at six.","My sister wakes up in six."],"answer":"My sister wakes up at six.","explanation":"he / she / it → verb + -s.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نضيف s للفعل."},{"q":"What time does your dad come home? – ___","options":["He come home at five.","He is come home in five.","He comes home at five.","He comes home on five."],"answer":"He comes home at five.","explanation":"he / she / it → verb + -s.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نضيف s للفعل."}],"theme_ar":"روتيني اليومي","essential_question_ar":"كيف يساعدنا الروتين الجيد كل يوم؟","can_do":"I can describe my day and other people's days with the present simple and tell the time.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أصف يومي ويوم الآخرين بالمضارع البسيط وأن أخبر عن الوقت."});
